RO: Ce va afisa procesul parinte in consola?

EN: What will the parent process display in the console?

int main() {
    int p[2], n = 11;
    pipe(p);

    close p[1]);
    if (fork() == 0) {          //child process
        close(p[0]);
        n = 7;
        write([p[1], &n, sizeof(int));
        close(p[1]);
        exit(0);
    }

    read(p[0], &n, sizeof(int));
    close(p[0];
    printf("%d\n", n");

    return 0;
}

Answer:
The write end of pipe is closed before entering in the child process, that means that the child process can write in the pipe and then in the parent process the read will see end of file and will return 0, so the value of n wont be changed, and at the end the value 11 will be printed.
